# Directives set by hand in the Catapult GUI for QMlp_Slim (2026-10-26).
#
# Source: the solution's directives.tcl,
#   SmtPxl_QMlp_Slim_io_parallel_Latency_pw_hls4ml_prj/SmtPxl_QMlp_Slim_prj/
#   SmtPxl_QMlp_Slim.v1/directives.tcl
# (lines between "go assembly" and "go architect"). The whole file is kept
# next to this one as QMlp_Slim_full_directives.tcl.
#
# Setup: Catapult 2024.2_2, model fingerprint 392456de (1000 + 2000 epochs),
# io_parallel, Latency, programmable weights (_pw), ReuseFactor 1, 25 ns
# clock, TSMC 28nm tcbn28hpcplusbwp30p140ssg0p81v125c_ccs_dc. The project
# was generated by codesign_catapult.ipynb with Synth = False, so
# build_prj.tcl stopped after go compile; these were applied after
# go assembly, then the flow was run to go extract.
#
# Result: latency 2 cycles, throughput 1 cycle, total area score
# 335,053.2 (post-assignment), slack 15.72 ns. See PLAN.md,
# "QMlp_Slim Catapult results".
#
# Contents:
# - every layer output, the two pooling buffers and the six dense
#   accumulators mapped to registers
# - main loop pipelined with II=1 (one result per clock)
# - every other loop fully unrolled
#
# To reuse: open the project (catapult -f build_prj.tcl), then in the
# Catapult transcript run "go assembly", "source <this file>" and
# "go extract". The paths name hls4ml layer numbers and template
# arguments, so they only fit this model; other models (e.g.
# QConv1D_Slim) need their own list.

